---
layout: base.njk
title: Independent Mac apps & browser tools
description: Meet RelayByte, the independent software studio of Kyle Reddoch. Discover Trayage for Mac, Drift for Chrome, and StylePort for Safari.
home: true
ogVideo: true
---
<section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Independent software. Personal by design.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Good software.<br><span class="accent-text">Less friction.</span></h1>
      <p>A tidier Mac. A browser that feels like yours. A good find, shared. Small apps that make the everyday a little better.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="#apps">Meet the apps <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}">Read the blog <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <p class="hero-signature">Built with care by Kyle Reddoch, in Texas.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="studio-visual">
      <span class="orbit orbit-one" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="orbit orbit-two" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <button class="brand-art" type="button" aria-label="RelayByte logo card" disabled>
        <span class="brand-art-tilt"><span class="brand-art-spinner">
          <span class="brand-art-face brand-art-front"><span class="art-label" aria-hidden="true">MADE OF SMALL IDEAS.</span><img src="{{ '/assets/brand/relaybyte-symbol-orange.svg' | url }}" alt="" width="512" height="512"><span class="art-foot"><span aria-hidden="true">BUILT TO BE USEFUL.</span><span class="art-cta" id="brand-card-action" hidden><span class="art-action-text">Give it a spin</span><span class="art-action-icon" aria-hidden="true">↻</span></span></span></span>
          <span class="brand-art-face brand-art-back" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ '/assets/brand/relaybyte-symbol-orange.svg' | url }}" alt="" width="512" height="512"></span>
        </span></span>
      </button>
      <div class="orbit-app orbit-trayage" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ '/assets/apps/trayage.png' | url }}" alt="" width="80" height="80"><span>Trayage<small>A little more order.</small></span></div>
      <div class="orbit-app orbit-styleport" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ '/assets/apps/styleport.png' | url }}" alt="" width="64" height="64"></div>
      <div class="orbit-app orbit-drift" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ '/assets/apps/drift.svg' | url }}" alt="" width="48" height="48"><span>Drift<small>Worth sharing.</small></span></div>
      <span class="visual-caption">A small studio. A growing collection.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="studio-principles"><span>Thoughtfully small.</span><span>Clear about your data.</span><span>A real person behind every app.</span></div>
</section>
<section class="apps-section shell" id="apps" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">The collection</p><h2 id="apps-title">A little better,<br>one app at a time.</h2></div><p>Different ideas. The same care.<br>Find something that fits your day.</p></div>
  <article class="featured-product" aria-labelledby="featured-trayage">
    <div class="featured-copy"><div class="feature-identity"><img src="{{ '/assets/apps/trayage.png' | url }}" alt="" width="64" height="64"><div><h3 id="featured-trayage">Trayage</h3><span>macOS 14+ · Available now</span></div></div><h4>Your Downloads.<br>Back in perspective.</h4><p>Installers, possible duplicates, and files you’ve forgotten about. See what’s there, review what matters, and decide what stays.</p><div class="feature-links"><a class="button button-dark" href="https://trayage.app/download/" data-tinylytics-event="app.download" data-tinylytics-event-value="https://trayage.app/download/">Download Trayage <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/apps/trayage/' | url }}">About Trayage <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="feature-note">Free file review. Optional cleanup trial.<br>Direct download and Mac App Store.</p></div>
    <figure class="featured-screen"><div class="screen-topline"><span>LESS CLUTTER. MORE CLARITY.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><img src="{{ '/assets/apps/trayage-review.webp' | url }}" alt="Trayage’s native review window groups Downloads files and explains why a selected file appears. Shown with sample files." width="1400" height="967"><figcaption>Real app. Sample files. Your decisions.</figcaption></figure>
  </article>
  <div class="secondary-products">{% for app in apps %}{% if app.slug != 'trayage' %}
    <article class="small-product small-product-{{ app.slug }}" aria-labelledby="home-{{ app.slug }}"><div class="small-product-top"><img src="{{ app.icon | url }}" alt="" width="72" height="72"><span class="product-status">{{ app.status }}</span></div><p class="eyebrow">{{ app.platform }}</p><h3 id="home-{{ app.slug }}">{{ app.name }}</h3><h4>{{ app.line }}</h4><p>{{ app.description }}</p><div class="small-product-links"><a class="text-link" href="{{ app.url }}" data-tinylytics-event="{{ app.event }}" data-tinylytics-event-value="{{ app.url }}">{{ app.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="product-detail-link" href="{{ ('/apps/' + app.slug + '/') | url }}">About {{ app.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}</div>
  <div class="section-tail"><span>Useful on their own. Made with the same care.</span><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/apps/' | url }}">Explore the collection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</section>
<section class="maker-band"><div class="maker-section shell" aria-labelledby="maker-title"><p class="eyebrow">Independent, on purpose</p><div class="maker-grid"><div><h2 id="maker-title">A small studio.<br>A real person.</h2><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">Meet the maker <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div><p>I’m Kyle Reddoch, an independent developer in Texas. RelayByte is where I turn the things I wish worked a little better into apps you can actually use.</p><p>My background in cybersecurity shapes the details: clear controls, sensible defaults, and an honest explanation of what happens to your data.</p><span class="maker-signature">Kyle Reddoch <span>/ Founder & developer</span></span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="journal-section shell" aria-labelledby="journal-title"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">From the studio</p><h2 id="journal-title">The work behind<br>the work.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}">Read all notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="journal-home-grid"><div class="journal-posts">{% include 'post-list.njk' %}</div><div class="journal-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Building in the open</span><h3>The decisions.<br>The experiments.<br>The lessons.</h3><p>A look at what goes into making independent software, from the first idea to the details that make it useful.</p><a class="journal-rss" href="{{ '/blog/feed.xml' | url }}">Follow via RSS <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="home-faq shell" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</p><h2 id="faq-title">Good to know.</h2><a class="text-link" href="{{ '/support/' | url }}">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="faq-list">{% for item in faq %}<details><summary>{{ item.question }}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{{ item.answer }}</p></details>{% endfor %}</div></section>
